tags: launch-load, launch_scarcity

A promise of the node: the load of each resource at which the node computed the price
of the offer. A caller can compute the price at the launch with it.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key. The key is the id of the formal of a
resource (cpu, disk or memory), and the value is the load of that resource in
millionths, from 0 to 1000000, in base 10.

With no promise, the caller does not know the load. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
load=for each resource in resources: the part of the capacity of the node that is in use, in millionths, as the node measures it
